# Evidence Room public repo — exclusion contract.
#
# This gitignore is BELT; the staging script (prepare.ps1) is SUSPENDERS: blocked content
# is never copied into this tree in the first place, and this file stops it if someone
# copies by hand later. From the 2026-08-17 public-release audit.

# Raw fetched data. NOT re-fetchable by construction, and the earlier claim that it was
# is withdrawn: on 2026-08-31 a second machine tried to rebuild from a clean clone and
# could not. Two independent reasons. Sixty-five producer scripts existed only in the
# internal tree, so several published pages had no path from source to page at all
# (seven were added that day; the rest produce withheld pages and stay out). And of the
# fetchers that WERE here, fetch_oews.py takes a 403 from BLS and
# fetch_odjfs_projections.py fails TLS verification, so a page can be un-rebuildable
# even with every script present. Treat a rebuild as something to TEST, never assert.
#
# The build cache itself is shared between machines through a private repository, not
# this one: github.com/polymerindustrycluster/evidence-room-data (see _data/REBUILDING.md). What stays out of here permanently is below, on the merits
# rather than on re-fetchability:
# (_sbir_awards.csv carries PI emails; ohsos_bulk.json carries SoS filing records;
# metroverse.json is CC BY-NC-SA + D&B-derived and may NEVER enter a public repo.)
_data/build/*.json
_data/build/*.jsonl
_data/build/*.csv
_data/build/*.zip
_data/build/*.xlsx
_data/build/*.txt
_data/build/__pycache__/

# Internal process docs stay internal. Two exceptions ship: METHODS-SOP.md, the public
# methods doc, and REBUILDING.md, which records which pages a stranger can actually
# rebuild and which they cannot. The second is only useful in public.
_data/*.md
!_data/METHODS-SOP.md
!_data/REBUILDING.md

# Staging machinery is process, not product.
stage/

# Vault-serving prototype (sqlite with 1,834 companies + member table).
_data/prototype-sqlite/

# QA scratch renders — six embed blocked pages.
shots/
*/shots/

# Licensed fonts (Aptos — Microsoft). Code may name the font; files never ship.
# The rule is about REDISTRIBUTION RIGHTS, not about fonts, so an OFL face that the site
# is required to ship is an exception rather than a relaxation. Added 2026-08-31: the
# shared sheet named Lato and shipped nothing, so every reader without Lato installed got
# fallback metrics and no true 900 weight. Lato is SIL OFL 1.1 (see _shared/fonts/OFL.txt),
# redistributable with its notice, 51 KB across six woff2 subsets. Aptos stays blocked:
# it is ttf/otf and is not exempted below.
*/fonts/
*.ttf
*.otf
!_shared/fonts/
!_shared/fonts/*.woff2
!_shared/fonts/OFL.txt

# Bundles are built in CI for the shipped set only — a committed dist/ was a standing
# leak vector (contaminated + font-embedded bundles found in the audit).
dist/

# Withheld artifacts — ALL TEN. See README "Not in this repository".
# This list must match $BLOCKED in stage/prepare.ps1 exactly. It was short by four for a
# day: collaboration, credit, reach and talent were held on 2026-08-17 and only the staging
# allowlist was updated, so the belt had gaps the suspenders happened to cover. Two guards
# only work if both are complete.
chain/
rfq/
trl/
oversubscribed/
6ppd/
ledger/
collaboration/
credit/
reach/
talent/

.env
node_modules/
__pycache__/
